            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for an omen, then the Tamil for prudence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: பங்குச்சந்தை",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பங்குச்சந்தை — paṅkuccantai — \"the stock market\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பங்குச்சந்தை சரிந்தால் பலர் பணத்தை இழப்பார்கள். paṅkuccantai carintāl palar paṇattai iḻappārkaḷ. If the stock market falls, many people will lose money."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Word for word \"share market\": பங்கு \"a share\" + சந்தை (cantai)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பங்குச்சந்தை (paṅkuccantai) is a modern compound: the native பங்கு (paṅku), \"a share, a portion\", from பகு, \"to divide\" (DEDR 3808), and சந்தை (cantai), \"a market\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
